{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization (514 audited declarations, zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only) resolving all four questions and observations (Q1, Q2, O1, O2) from Badkobeh and Ochem (Theoret. Comput. Sci. 588, 2015) for the 5-letter morphic fixed point b5 = f5^omega(0) (0 -> 01, 1 -> 23, 2 -> 4, 3 -> 21, 4 -> 0). The library identifies b5 as the exact 5-interval coding of a golden-ratio 3-interval exchange on (-phi^2/2, phi^3/2) via the -1/phi left eigenvector, proving unconditionally that (Q1) b5 has exact factor complexity 4n + 1 for every n >= 0, (O1) g_fib(b5) has the exact same factors as the Fibonacci word with complexity n + 1, (O2) g_rf(b5) has the exact same factors as the Rote-Fibonacci word with complexity 2n for n >= 1, and (Q2) the critical exponent of b5 is exactly (5 + sqrt(5))/4 and is strictly unattained. It also proves the sharp second-order bound |w|/p < (5 + sqrt(5))/4 - (7 - sqrt(5))/(8p) with exact unattained deficit infimum (7 - sqrt(5))/4, asymptotic critical exponent E*(b5) = (5 + sqrt(5))/4, irrationality of E(b5), reversal-swap (3 <-> 4) language invariance, ternary 3-IET collapse complexity 2n + 1, unbounded balance defect, and the exact 5th-order A005252 length recurrence. Companion manuscript and verification archive: https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/badkobeh-ochem-word-b5.",
